Transit Student Organizations Athletics Blue Devil Bands Greek Life Student Veterans Group Student Government Blue Devil Motorsports Student Support Career Services Clinical Counseling Office of International Programs One Stop Center Student Access and Accommodations Student Accounts LGBT Resource Center ABOUT Contact Us Campus Map Directions Facilities Consumer Information Office of the President Marketing Job Openings Faculty and Staff Resources Employee Handbooks Faculty and Staff Directory Organizational Chart Staff Senate Human Resources 25Live Title IX Community Programs Facility Rental High School Summer Programs Marburger STEM Center Robofest History NEWS CALENDAR ALUMNI GIVING FACULTY + STAFF BANNERWEB EHELP Search Job Postings Home » Job Postings » Clinical Education Assistant for PA Program Clinical Education Assistant for PA Program Date Posted: June 23, 2026 Position Number: CI9909 Hiring Supervisor: Director of the Physician Assistant Program Job Type: Staff Employment Type: Full-Time » Job Description JOB TITLE: Clinical Education Assistant for PA Program POSITION NUMBER: CI9909 HIRING SUPERVISOR: Director of the Physician Assistant Program DEPARTMENT: Physician Assistant TYPE: Full-Time SUMMARY: The key responsibility of this position is the planning, preparation, and successful process of clinical rotations for Physician Assistant students and possibly for Nursing students. This position consults, collaborates and plans activities with the PA Director of Clinical Education (DCE), Program Directors, and external clinical partners. This position communicates effectively with students and responds to their needs and concerns. This position works with faculty members, the program directors, and all other key stakeholders including affiliated hospitals, medical practices, preceptors, and partners to and coordinate compliance paperwork for specific clinical placement requirements and to ensure preceptor vetting and communication. JOB DUTIES: 1) Clinical Administration Collaborates with the PA Director of Clinical Education, Program Director, and clinical coordinators to obtain specific student clinical requirements, then uses the information to accurately coordinate plans, and manage assigned tasks for clinical placements for students required to meet graduation criteria Forecasts clinical placement requirements based on student enrollment data and coordinate with directors the scheduling of the clinical placements well in advance Communicates with clinical sites to obtain and manage the required documents and assures they are all current and acquired as needed Responds to requests from the PA DCE, Program directors, and clinical coordinators to change or modify placements. Engages actively with clinical coordinators to establish and maintain successful relationships, including site visits as required Develops and implements innovative approaches to improve methods of clinical placement and obtaining compliance documents Assist with onboarding and training of students to the clinical database system Responsible for the coordination of the PA students’ ‘end of rotation days’ clinical activities and assist as required and possibly with the Nursing Program’s activities Collaborate with the program coordinators to assure a smooth interface between the clinical and didactic phases of the program Assist with other programs’ activities as required 2) Database Management Schedule student clinical placements in the used database platform & spreadsheets Routinely maintains updates of clinical sites and preceptors Executes rotation requests into ACEMAPP database when necessary Maintains and oversees applicable preceptors payments on an ongoing basis Train and become a source expert on platforms related to the program and clinical year 3) Administrative Attend all team meetings and other meetings as required including the annual faculty retreat Provides meeting minutes with clinical year team meetings Collaborate with the clinical coordinators from affiliated hospitals and clinical sites to assure effective communication Identifies all preceptor payments and monitors payment activities to assure timely stipends are processed (or continued medical education credits) as applicable Assists the PA DCE, program directors, and clinical faculty in updating handbooks, documents, etc. as assigned Coordinate obtaining electronic and/or handwritten evaluations and documents as assigned, and processes all information related to clinical rotations in the database platform as required Collaboratively create and maintain a preceptor recognition process 4) Other duties as assigned per the Program Director EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE: The ideal candidate will have earned an associate’s/bachelor’s degree or higher, have 2+ years prior experience in healthcare management and/or administrative experience and experience within a higher education institution. This candidate is highly organized, can work under short deadlines, multitask and manage multiple competing and changing priorities smoothly. They will be proficient in word processing, spreadsheet creation and management, and specific software applications as required. Must be willing to take initiative, be proactive related to the needs of the students and program and open to new ideas. This position requires a flexible schedule to assure the needs of the program are met. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to maintain professional relationships with clinical partners Possesses professional communications skills, both written and verbal Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and manage time to meet established deadlines Ability to make decisions within the university’s policies and procedures Self-motivated and willing to take on new projects Able to work independently and collaboratively Excellent attention to detail Database management experience required Experience using a database such as Exxat, Typhon, Complio, and ACEMAPP ideal, but not required Must have a valid driver’s license or  reliable transportation to travel to work sites. Lawrence Technological University (LTU) conducts pre-employment screening on initial candidates for all positions, which may include but is not limited to, a criminal background check, verification of academic credentials, license, certifications, and/or verification of work history.  Lawrence Technological University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. » How to Apply Applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and three references with contact information to paprogram@ltu.edu . Consideration of applications begins immediately and continues through June 30, 2026. 1 800 225 5588 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI, 48075-1058 Instagram Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Facebook-f X-twitter Tiktok Linkedin Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Quick Links News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library Admissions Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Life Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library About Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy ©2026 Lawrence Technological University. All Rights Reserved. Title IX Sitemap Title IX Sitemap"
