teous customer service. The employee must perform assigned duties promptly and professionally, follow University and departmental procedures, and comply with lawful and supervisory instructions. Mail Services operates under the Department of Campus Safety, and this position reports to the Mail Services Supervisor. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Follow established procedures and supervisory direction for receiving, processing, documenting, sorting, distributing, and delivering mail and packages. Maintain accurate and timely records, including package tracking, transfers, deliveries, and discrepancies; promptly report missing, damaged, or misdirected items. Protect the confidentiality, security, and integrity of mail, packages, records, and related information; prevent unauthorized access or tampering. Collect and distribute mail and packages to appropriate departments, residence halls, and recipients; coordinate pickups and deliveries with courier services. Operate University vehicles and mail-processing equipment safely; obey traffic regulations and report equipment, vehicle, and workplace hazards promptly. Maintain supplies and a clean, orderly, and safe mailroom; use proper lifting and material handling practices. Provide courteous assistance and accurate information to faculty, staff, students, and visitors. Complete assigned duties accurately and within established timeframes; promptly advise the supervisor of delays, operational problems, or needed assistance. Maintain professional and cooperative working relationships; observe attendance, punctuality, and scheduled-work requirements under University policy. Notify Campus Safety promptly of observed campus safety hazards or incidents. Perform other related duties, including appropriate assistance with University events or emergencies, consistent with training, qualifications, and safety procedures. QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS: Must be at least 18 years old and legally authorized to work in the United States. Must possess and maintain a valid Michigan driver’s license and an acceptable driving record when driving is required. Must meet applicable background-screening requirements, maintain a neat professional appearance, and be available for schedule adjustments or overtime as operationally necessary and determined by the Executive Director of Campus Safety or his designee. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: High school diploma or equivalent required. Prior experience in mail services, shipping and receiving, logistics, inventory tracking, or customer service preferred. LANGUAGE SKILLS: Ability to read and follow written procedures, safety instructions, and operational records; communicate clearly and respectfully in person, in writing, and by telephone or radio. REASONING ABILITY: Ability to exercise sound judgment, resolve routine problems, recognize discrepancies, prioritize assignments, and seek supervisory guidance when necessary. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Work involves standing, walking, climbing stairs, bending, kneeling, reaching, sitting, driving, and repetitive hand use. May occasionally lift or move packages weighing up to 75 pounds, using appropriate assistance or equipment when needed. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Ability to work independently while following supervisory direction; use computers, scanners, tracking systems, and mail-processing equipment; maintain accurate records; protect confidential information; and demonstrate reliability, professionalism, and a service-oriented attitude. WORK ENVIRONMENT: Work is performed in mailroom, campus, vehicle, and outdoor settings, including varying weather conditions. During winter months, the mailroom may experience significantly reduced indoor temperatures due to the frequent opening and closing of the delivery door. This is an inherent and unavoidable condition of normal mailroom operations, and employees are expected to dress appropriately for these temperature fluctuations, consistent with University dress and safety requirements. Occasional exposure to moving equipment and moderate noise may occur. Lawrence Technological University (LTU) conducts pre-employment screening on initial candidates for all positions, which may include but is not limited to, a criminal background check, verification of academic credentials, license, certifications, and/or verification of work history.  Lawrence Technological University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. » How to Apply Please send cover letter and resume to Michael Killingbeck at mkillingb@ltu.edu . 1 800 225 5588 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI, 48075-1058 Instagram Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Facebook-f X-twitter Tiktok Linkedin Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Quick Links News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library Admissions Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Life Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library About Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy ©2026 Lawrence Technological University. All Rights Reserved. Title IX Sitemap Title IX Sitemap"
    },
