editation Faculty Policies Registrar’s Office Tuition and Fee Information Registration and Scheduling Record Requests Update Academic and Personal Information Non-Attendance Process Forms to Print Graduation Degree Requirements Commencement Ceremony Graduating Student Survey RESEARCH Office of the Sr. VP of Research and Economic Development Research Projects Research Centers For Researchers For Business and Industry For University Partners STUDENT LIFE Dean of Students Student Code of Conduct University Policies Campus Bookstore Blue Devil Perks Campus Safety Dining Services Housing Tech Transit Student Organizations Athletics Blue Devil Bands Greek Life Student Veterans Group Student Government Blue Devil Motorsports Student Support Career Services Clinical Counseling Office of International Programs One Stop Center Student Access Student Accounts LGBT Resource Center ABOUT Contact Us Campus Map Directions Facilities Consumer Information Office of the President Marketing Job Openings Faculty and Staff Resources Employee Handbooks Faculty and Staff Directory Organizational Chart Staff Senate Human Resources 25Live Title IX Community Programs Facility Rental High School Summer Programs Marburger STEM Center Robofest History NEWS CALENDAR ALUMNI GIVING FACULTY + STAFF BANNERWEB EHELP Search Job Postings Home » Job Postings » Clinical Counselor (Licensed) Clinical Counselor (Licensed) Date Posted: October 22, 2026 Position Number: CC9995 Hiring Supervisor: Dean of Students Job Type: Staff Employment Type: Full-Time Department: Student Affairs » Job Description JOB TITLE: Clinical Counselor (Licensed) POSITION NUMBER : CC9995 HIRING SUPERVISOR: Dean of Students DEPARTMENT: Student Affairs TYPE: Full-Time SUMMARY: A full time staff member within the Division of Student Affairs who works to provide counseling services and education outreach to currently enrolled students on Lawrence Tech’s campus. Counselors assist students with a wide range of behavioral, developmental, and mental health concerns in support of personal growth and academic success. ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES: Work is expected to include approximately 60% direct service (counseling and outreach) and 30% indirect service (administrative tasks, planning, consultation, supervision). Provide counseling services for students at the university, including short-term psychotherapy, group therapy, crisis intervention, and mental health screenings. Experience and previous work with student athlete populations and/or neurodivergent student populations is beneficial. Provide mental health focused workshops and programs to various campus stakeholders (faculty, staff, and/or students). Outreach may consist of planned programming or developed in response to events impacting the campus community. Participate in tabling events to increase awareness of counseling services on campus. Support the department in development of electronic outreach including social media marketing. Participate in university events which could include: orientation, open houses, convocation, graduation, athletic events, and/or mandatory trainings as needed/required. Participate in Campus Assessment, Response, and Evaluation (CARE) team when needed to insure student welfare and campus safety. Response to urgent/emergency situations on campus which can occasionally include day, evening, and weekend hours. Develop relationships and collaborate with departments across campus including Career Services, Housing, Office of Access and Accommodations, Athletics, Student Success Center, and Academic departments. Participate in committees as assigned on an on-going or needed basis. Participate in Clinical Counseling staff meetings, clinical, and/or employment supervision as needed. Utilizes counseling center’s electronic health record system for scheduling and documentation. Completes other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS AND EDUCATION: Master’s degree from an accredited college or university in clinical psychology, counseling, or social work with a limited or full Michigan license in psychology, social work, or counseling. Candidates will be expected to receive a full/independent Michigan license within 3 years of hire and are expected to maintain licensure for the duration of employment. 1-3 years of clinical counseling experience, preference will be given to those with experience in higher education and university counseling center settings. Competence in working with multicultural and other diverse populations including international student populations. Demonstrated ability to work autonomously and collaboratively, strong communication skills, as well as commitment to workplace integrity and professional ethics. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodations. COMMENTS: While acting as a representative of Lawrence Technological University, it is important that the employee be knowledgeable and professional. Communication skills (both oral and written), organizational skills, and the ability to handle changing priorities are essential for success in this position. The position may require evening and some weekends (Saturday or Sunday) to serve the needs of the LTU community. Lawrence Technological University (LTU) conducts pre-employment screening on initial candidates for all positions, which may include but is not limited to, a criminal background check, verification of academic credentials, license, certifications, and/or verification of work history.  Lawrence Technological University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. » How to Apply Please send cover letter and resume to Kimberly Jerdine at kjerdine@ltu.edu . 1 800 225 5588 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI, 48075-1058 Instagram Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Facebook-f X-twitter Tiktok Linkedin Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Quick Links News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library News Calendar Alumni Giving F